title: Dig
---
<<once>>
    <<enable_UI Commands DigInstruction>>
<<endonce>>
===

title: SkullIntro
---
<<once>>
    ???: Who goes there?
    <<show_fire Fire>>
    <<set_fire_animation Fire grow>>
    <<set_fire_animation Fire fall>>
    <<set_fire_animation Fire grow>>
    <<wait 0.5>>
    <<set_fire_animation Fire knight>>
    <<wait 2.0>>
    ???: Brave hero, have you come for the ultimate weapon to slay a demon?
    <<set_fire_animation Fire med>>
    <<wait 2.0>>
    ???: Or for the antidote to an incurable disease?
    <<set_fire_animation Fire lady>>
    <<wait 2.0>>
    ???: Or perhaps, are you the dashing savior here to rescue me from my chains?
    ???: Tell me, what are you here for?
    // <<set_light_intensity SpotLight 0.5>>
    <<fade_light GlobalLight 1.0>>
    <<fade_light PlayerLight 1.0>>
    ???: ...
    ???: Ah. Not another hopeless one. 
    <<hide_fire Fire>>
    <<show_skull Skull>>
    <<fade_light SkullLight 1>>
    I suggest you turn back, small one. This is no place to wander alone.
    <<wait 1.0>>
    <<set_skull_animation Skull bored>>
    ...
    <<wait 1.0>>
    <<set_skull_animation Skull exasp>>
    ... 
    (Can it understand me?)
    (Or is it feigning ignorance?)
    // <optional: dog itch>
    <<set_skull_animation Skull angry>>
    (Gah! A touch nut to crack, I see).
    ???: Out with it! Do you have a wish or not?
    <<set_dog_animation Dog bark>>
    <<wait 1.0>>
    <<set_skull_animation Skull neutral>>
    ???: Oh? 
    ???: I suppose it is odd for a lowly creature like yourself to end up here, all alone.
    ???: What are you searching for, small one?
    <<set_skull_animation Skull bored>>
    ???: What have you lost?
    <<set_dog_animation Dog sad>>
    <<wait 1.0>>
    ???: ...
    <<set_skull_animation Skull neutral>>
    ???: Well, worry not. Whatever it is, I can help you find it.
    <<set_dog_animation Dog wag>>
    <<wait 1.0>>
    ???: As soon as you help me with one small favor, that is.
    ???: Come with me.
    <<play_timeline CutsceneTrigger2>>
<<endonce>>
===

title: FetchBone
---
<<once>>
    <<declare $numBones =  3>>
    <<declare $hasBone = false>>
    ???: Er, so--I need you to fetch my bones.
    //optional: sound effect or dog cock head
    <<wait 1.0>>
    <<enable_UI Commands FireMap>>
    ???: Long ago, certain enemies of mine scattered my bones all over this domain.
    ???: I've managed to recoup most of them over the years, but a few have remained in the clutches of pesky tomb raiders, just out of my reach. //exasperated
    ???: Find my missing bones and drop them in this pit.
    ???: Lucky for both of us, they're my smallest bones, so they should be doable for a being of your... stature.
    <<disable_UI Commands FireMap>>
<<endonce>>
<<disable_collider Scene1_BoundL>>
===

title: FoundBone
---
???: I feel my power returning...
<<jump BonesMap>>
===

title: BonesMap
---
<<if $numBones < 3>>
    <<if $hasBone>>
        ???: Splendid! You found one!
        <<destroy_item Commands Phalange>>
        <<set $hasBone to false>>
        <<set_skull_animation Skull bored>>
        ???: Ah, I can feel my power returning.
        <<set_skull_animation Skull neutral>>
        <<enable_UI Commands FireMap>>
        {$numBones} bones left to find.
        <<disable_UI Commands FireMap>>
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    ???: Hurry along now, go find my missing bones.
    <<enable_UI Commands FireMap>>
    {$numBones} bones left to find.
    <<disable_UI Commands FireMap>>
<<endif>>



===

title: Bone1Start
---
<<once>>
    ???: See those holes?
    ???: One of them has my phalange. Dig to unearth it.
    Press X while standing next to a dark patch to dig
<<endonce>>
===

title: Bone1After
---
<<once>>
    ???: Well done! Now take it back to the pit.
    Press C to pick up
    <<set $numBones to $numBones - 1>>
<<endonce>>
===

title: AllBonesDone
---
???: Ah, at last. All my bones are reunited.
//xolotl materializes from whole skeleton
???: Surprised to see a fellow canine?
???: I am taking this form to be more easily comprehensible to you. Getting on your level, so to speak.
Xolotl: My name is Xolotl. I thank you for restoring my power.
Xolotl: As promised, I will grant you any wish, as long as it is in my ability. 
Xolotl: Tell me, what is your wish?
<<set_dog_animation Dog bark>>
Xolotl: Hmm? A lost girl, you say?
Xolotl: That can be arranged. Do you have a strong memory of this girl? One that carries an intense emotion, whether that be happiness, sadness, anger.
Xolotl: Close your eyes. Picture it in your head.
//dog close eyes
//overlay anim of smile, hands outstretched for hug, throwing toy
Xolotl: Yes, the joy in this memory should do nicely for locating her soul.
//stone appears
//Xolotl moves towards it
Xolotl: ...I see.
Xolotl: This girl is no longer in the world of the living.
//dog sad
Xolotl: At least, her soul is not. But her physical body appears to be alive and unharmed.
Xolotl: But you already knew that, didn't you? //narrow eyes
//dog whines
Xolotl: Unfortunately, the girl is in a unique state. She can only return to the world of the living if she chooses. No one else can make that choice for her.
Xolotl: I'm sorry, little one. I cannot help you.
<<jump HuehueIntro>>
===

title: HuehueIntro
---
???: What the heck, Xolo!
//coyote appears
???: Here you are harping on about being able to grant any wish!
Xolotl: You again, Coyote.
Coyote?: Grr, use my full name, won't ya? It's Huehuecoyotl to you! Hue-hue-coyotl!
Huehuecoyotl: This pup needs help. Isn't it our job to help the denizens of Tlaltipac?
Xolotl: We cannot disrupt the balance of life and death, Coyote. 
Huehuecoyotl: What, scared of your big brother?
//X annoyed, shakes it off
Xolotl: If we bring one soul back, the floodgates will open and I will be powerless to stop it. You know that.
Xolotl: Besides, either of us entering the Dream Mind of a single human would cause it to shatter.
Huehuecoyotl: WE can't intervene in human affairs. But that doesn't mean HE can't.
Huehuecoyotl: Why don't we have this pup enter her Dream Mind? He's not a god so it should be fine, right?
Xolotl: What? He's just a little dog. Frankly, I'm still not sure how he is got here.
Xolotl: The Dream Mind is a dangerous place. If he were to descend, the chances are high that he would not come back.
<<set_dog_animation Dog bark>>
Xolotl: What? You want to do it, knowing the risks?
Huehuecoyotl: That's the spirit, pup!
//dog wags tail
Xolotl: That's absurd. But...
Xolotl: With the strength of his resolve, perhaps he has a chance to reach her. 
Xolotl: But why do you care what happens to this little dog and his human?
Huehuecoyotl: Honestly, I just love the drama! This well-ordered world of yours is so boring sometimes. That's why I try to stir up a little excitement from time to time!
Huehuecoyotl: Plus, I'm imagining Quetzalcoatl's face when he finds out about this. Heehee!
Xolotl: Sigh. No guarantees, but I will let you try, little one.
Xolotl: Come take a look at this stone slab.
<<jump MindSurface>>
===

title: MindSurface
---
//dog moves closer
//overlay: grooves on stone
Xolotl: This is your girl's Mind Surface.
Xolotl: See these pits? These represent the places she frequents most in her subconscious.
Xolotl: The deeper the pit, the more time she has spent there.
//marbles scatter onto surface and start spinning around
Xolotl: You see, the mind really is a bunch of marbles, which roll around and catch on invisible things on the Mind Surface. 
Xolotl: In a healthy mind, the marbles roam freely, covering lots of ground.
//a marble starts circulating in one certain spot>
Xolotl: A marble may circle over the same path for a little while, which deepens the trench. That increases the activation energy needed for the marble to break out with its own momentum.
//marble breaks out>
Xolotl: Normally, this is not a problem, as the human mind is full of distractions. Distractions give the marbles enough energy to break out and explore other areas.
//one marble starts circling
Xolotl: However, occasionally, a marble does not receive enough energy to break free of its orbit. Eventually, it carves itself deeper into the Mind Surface, to the point that it can no longer escape. 
Xolotl: This usually means there are troubles the human is fixating on. The more they fixate and overthink, the more gravity those troubles build up, and they become even more irresistible to think about.
//<one marble sinks deeper into stone>
Huehuecoyotl: in other words, a vicious cycle, huh?
Xolotl: Yes. 
Xolotl: Your task, little one, is to dive into these pits and extricate the marbles lodged there. Then, I can restore the surface to a flat state.
Xolotl: There are four major pits. We shall target this one first.
Huehuecoyotl: Why that one? There's only one marble in there.
Xolotl: I doubt the little one can handle the deeper pits yet. There is no point charging ahead only to fail immediately.
Huehuecoyotl: Hmph, always so careful.
Xolotl: Well, little one? Shall I send you to the first pit?
<<set_dog_animation Dog bark>>
Xolotl: brace yourself.
Huehuecoyotl: I'm rooting for ya, pup!
//<X howls. Dog envelopes in green light and floats in sky. Screen whites out>
===